---
globs:
  - "src/effect/**"
  - "src/webhook/**"
  - "src/state/intake.ts"
  - "src/commands/**"
  - "src/index.ts"
  - "test/architectureRules.test.ts"
---
One Node 24 process (`src/index.ts`) runs both the HTTP server (`src/effect/server.ts`) and the durable runtime (`src/agent/runtime/durable/boot.ts`), but intake stays cleanly separated from agent execution. The web module (`src/effect/server.ts`) serves `/health`, `/ready`, and `POST /webhooks` and does intake only: verify, parse, `toIntakeCommand` (`src/webhook/intakeCommand.ts`), then one `WebhookIntake.submit` into `src/state/intake.ts` (`BEGIN IMMEDIATE`) and `200` after commit. Bot identity and authorization lookups happen before opening the SQLite transaction. Reactions, progress stubs, slash replies, comments, checks, and labels run asynchronously via the dispatcher (`src/agent/runtime/durable/dispatcher.ts`). Work runs carry `installationId`; execution mints the token inside `PrSurface` (`src/github/prSurface.ts`). `test/architectureRules.test.ts` walks from `src/effect/server.ts` and fails if it reaches `src/agent/runtime/piSession.ts` or `modelsJson.ts`.
